{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["And others said: The reason for mentioning the flood is that, having mentioned part of His wonders—the descent of rain—He mentioned the immense wonder, namely the abundant rain in the days of Noah. This is a sign that HaShem sits enthroned from of old, and His lovingkindness is forever upon His people; therefore after it: 'YHWH will give strength to His people.'" "And some say: He mentioned the flood on account of the oath that the earth shall no more be destroyed, and the kingdom of HaShem—who is King of life—shall not be destroyed; therefore after it: 'And HaShem sits as King forever.'" "And some say: For from the day He sat to judge in the days of the flood, His kingship was seen, and the children of men who came after the flood feared, for before Noah there was no flood."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:54.320049240Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}